Message-ID: <T_MTlRtQ0KU._mb7cQ5gBgAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <T_MTlRtQ0KU.Dxh-hvQJBwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <T_MTlRtQ0KU.B5UlUoDsBwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com> <T_MTlRtQ0KU.Dxh-hvQJBwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/T_MTlRtQ0KU/m/_mb7cQ5gBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The output of scantwo is a list; the "lod" component is a matrix with the LOD score for the full model in the lower triangle and the LOD score for the additive model in the upper triangle. Get the interaction LOD score by subtraction. Here's an example:

data(hyper)
hyper <- calc.genoprob(hyper)
out <- scantwo(hyper, method="hk", verbose=FALSE)

lod.int <http://lod.int> <- out$lod - t(out$lod)
lod.int <http://lod.int>[upper.tri(lod.int <http://lod.int>)] <- t(lod.int <http://lod.int>)[upper.tri(lod.int <http://lod.int>)]

lod.int <http://lod.int>[1:5,1:5]

karl

